<!--
  Paper 1 (calibration), the CaMM operating point reported in Section V.

  This is ablation-ladder row 5 of data/archive_20260922/stair/run2.py, which
  EXPERIMENT_DESIGN.md 0.1 registers as "the paper's model" and which Donkey.Ning
  confirmed on 2026-09-28. Every real-data number in the manuscript comes from it.
  Reproduce the whole table with:
      python3 experiments/scripts/real_final_tables.py
  which reads this file rather than carrying its own copy of the settings.

  WHAT MAKES IT ROW 5 RATHER THAN ROW 7, and why that distinction cost a revision:

    k_search = 0 with delta_road = 300 m  => the disk is a FIXED 300 m circle, the
        same one the FMM baseline searches. Row 7 would be k_search = 1 with
        delta_road = 13.5 m, the HPL-adaptive disk, which belongs to paper 2
        (integrity) and is NOT what Section V reports. The two are easy to confuse
        and the candidate count is the tell: 8.82 candidates/epoch here, 2.92 there.
        Section III has described the fixed disk since the 2026-09-23 split, so a
        run with 2.92 candidates is not at the operating point this paper describes.

    phmi = 0  => the PHMI-grouped emission normalisation degenerates to a plain
        layer-wise softmax, which is Eq. (layer_norm) and nothing more. Paper 2
        carries the grouping. Note the two cannot be varied independently here:
        PHMI only has a boundary to group at because the disk is HPL-derived, so
        r and the grouping are one choice, and this is the choice the paper makes.

  THE TWO DIRECTION PARAMETERS ARE BOTH WRITTEN OUT, because they are the model's only
  calibrated constants and leaving one to a default is how a dataset-specific number
  becomes invisible:

    direction_kappa_scale = 0.227   c = 2(1-rho), the factor converting a one-epoch
        covariance into a two-epoch DIFFERENCE covariance. rho = 0.89 here.
    direction_kappa_floor = 0.0084  b, in rad^2: the heading variance the covariance
        cannot contain -- the vehicle's heading change within the epoch, the digitised
        centreline's disagreement with the road, the reference truth's noise. 5.5 deg.

  Both come from one regression, sigma_theta^2 = c * (n^T Sigma n)/|v|^2 + b, over
  11,792 correctly-matched gap-free steps (experiments/scripts/fit_direction_kappa.py).
  z(b) = 9.0, so the floor is real and not a fitting artefact. AN EARLIER VALUE OF
  c = 0.36 came from regressing on 1/|v|^2 alone, which omits the per-epoch regressor
  n^T Sigma n and is therefore biased; 0.227 is the definition this file uses, and the
  two are not two measurements of one quantity.

  THE CONSTANTS ARE A FIXED POINT, not a one-shot fit, and that is a property of the
  procedure rather than a refinement. The regression sample is "epochs the matcher got
  right on a gap-free step", so it depends on the matcher's parameters, which depend on
  the constants. Fitting against the previous configuration's output gives c = 0.254 /
  b = 0.0093; re-running at those and re-fitting gives 0.227 / 0.0084, and re-running at
  THOSE reproduces 0.227 / 0.0084 exactly. The iteration converges in one step and the
  values in this file are the converged ones. Two decimal places of agreement is not
  enough to skip the step: quoting a value the shipped configuration does not reproduce
  is the defect this comment exists to prevent.

  Why the floor matters even though it is only 3 % of the variance at highway speed:
  with it the concentration SATURATES at 1/b as |v| grows, so a long straight step
  cannot make the heading arbitrarily certain while the vehicle is steering. Removing
  the c term entirely and keeping only the floor costs 2.5 pp of accuracy on Haikou
  (98.14 -> 95.62), which is the clearest evidence that the term's value is in its
  SPEED DEPENDENCE and not in its magnitude.

  direction_max_interval = 2 s stays at its default: a gap guard, since a displacement
  spanning longer is not a heading. direction_symmetric stays false -- it is a measured
  net loss, see tests/test_cmm_direction_penalty.cpp.

  map_error_sigma = 10.6 m is sqrt(10^2 + 3.5^2): the paper's own decomposition of
  delta_road into 3.5 m of lane width and a 10 m map allowance, added in VARIANCE
  because the two sources are independent. A radius allowance is a worst case and
  adds linearly; a variance does not.
-->
<config>
  <input>
    <network>
      <file>input/map/hainan/edges.shp</file>
      <id>key</id>
      <source>u</source>
      <target>v</target>
    </network>
    <ubodt>
      <file>input/map/hainan_ubodt_indexed.bin</file>
    </ubodt>
    <gps>
      <file>data/real_vehicle/hainan_06/cmm_input_points_k1.csv</file>
      <id>id</id>
      <x>x</x>
      <y>y</y>
      <timestamp>timestamp</timestamp>
      <sde>sde</sde>
      <sdn>sdn</sdn>
      <sdu>sdu</sdu>
      <sdne>sdne</sdne>
      <sdeu>sdeu</sdeu>
      <sdun>sdun</sdun>
      <protection_level>protection_level</protection_level>
    </gps>
  </input>
  <output>
    <file>data/archive_20260928/final/cmm.csv</file>
    <fields>
      <point_mode/>
      <seq/>
      <timestamp/>
      <ogeom/>
      <cpath/>
      <tpath/>
      <opath/>
      <pgeom/>
      <ep/>
      <tp/>
      <trustworthiness/>
      <trustworthiness_smoothed/>
      <n_best_trustworthiness/>
      <candidates/>
      <status/>
      <delta_entropy/>
      <posterior_entropy/>
      <cumu_prob/>
    </fields>
  </output>
  <parameters>
    <k>16</k>
    <min_candidates>1</min_candidates>
    <reverse_tolerance>0.1</reverse_tolerance>
    <use_mahalanobis>true</use_mahalanobis>
    <filtered>true</filtered>
    <max_interval>180.0</max_interval>
    <trustworthiness_threshold>0.0</trustworthiness_threshold>
    <phmi>0.0</phmi>
    <cumulative_reverse_pct>0.03</cumulative_reverse_pct>
    <k_search>0.0</k_search>
    <delta_road>0.0026949335</delta_road>
    <map_error_sigma>10.6</map_error_sigma>
    <direction_kappa_scale>0.227</direction_kappa_scale>
    <direction_kappa_floor>0.0084</direction_kappa_floor>
  </parameters>
  <other>
    <log_level>2</log_level>
    <use_omp>true</use_omp>
    <input_epsg>4326</input_epsg>
  </other>
</config>
